      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Lip-sync workflow - read first",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Lip-sync to your own audio  (ref2va)\n\nThis is the **reference-to-video** task, a different model from the i2v workflow:\n`minimax_h3_ref2va_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors` (20.97 GB). Text encoder and both\nVAEs are shared, so that is the only extra file.\n\n## How it differs from the i2v workflow\n\n**There is no `first_frame`.** `MiniMaxH3ReferenceToVideo` has no first/last frame\ninputs. Your photo is `<Picture 1>` - an *identity reference* carried through the clip,\nnot an exact opening frame. The video will look like your subject; it will not start\non your image.\n\n**The prompt must use the tags.** References are addressed positionally as\n`<Picture 1>`, `<Audio 1>`, `<Video 1>`. Ordinals are 1-based per type and follow\nsocket order. If you add a second photo it becomes `<Picture 2>`.\n\n**The saved audio is YOUR song.** H3 always generates its own audio track, but for a\nmusic video that would hand you a re-synthesised approximation of your song. So\n`TrimAudioDuration` is wired straight into `CreateVideo`, and the model's audio branch\nis left out. The lips are synced against the reference; the file carries the real\ntrack.\n\nTo hear what the model actually generated instead, add a `VAEDecodeAudio`\n(samples <- sampler output, vae <- audio VAE) and feed that into `CreateVideo.audio`.\n\n## The 15 second wall\n\n362 frames / 15.08s is H3's trained maximum, so you cannot sync a whole song in one\npass. Work one segment at a time:\n\n- **`start_index`** on the Trim node picks *which* seconds of the song (e.g. `47.5`\n  for the chorus). It accepts negatives to count from the end.\n- **`duration` is preset-driven** and should be left connected - it is\n  `frames / 24`, so the audio always matches the video length exactly. Wire it by\n  hand only if you want a deliberate mismatch.\n\nTo build a longer music video, render several segments with sequential `start_index`\nvalues and concatenate them afterwards.\n\n## Presets\n\n| # | canvas | duration | tokens | notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **0** | manual | manual | - | use the three cyan manual nodes |\n| **1** | 768 x 768 | 5s (124 fr) | 21.3k | safest - square |\n| **2** | 1344 x 768 | 5s (124 fr) | 37.3k | max quality wide, 5s |\n| **3** | 864 x 480 | 10s (243 fr) | 29.2k | DEFAULT - 10s at 480p |\n| **4** | 960 x 544 | 10s (243 fr) | 36.7k | 10s, higher res |\n| **5** | 736 x 416 | 15s (362 fr) | 32.0k | safest 15s |\n| **6** | 864 x 480 | 15s (362 fr) | 43.3k | max duration - at the OOM edge |\n\n### Preset 0 - manual\n\nSet PRESET to `0` and the three cyan nodes take over; they are ignored otherwise.\n**manual: seconds** feeds the frame count *and* the audio trim from the same source,\nso the song segment still matches the video exactly in manual mode.\n\nSeconds snap **UP** to the next legal length - H3 only accepts `17k+5` frame counts,\nso durations land on a 0.7083s grid. Ask for 12.0s and you get 12.25s (294 frames).\n**8.000s (192 frames) is the only exactly-round length** in the usable range.\n\n| frames | secs | frames | secs | frames | secs |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 124 | 5.167 | 209 | 8.708 | 294 | 12.250 |\n| 141 | 5.875 | 226 | 9.417 | 311 | 12.958 |\n| 158 | 6.583 | 243 | 10.125 | 328 | 13.667 |\n| 175 | 7.292 | 260 | 10.833 | 345 | 14.375 |\n| **192** | **8.000** | 277 | 11.542 | 362 | 15.083 |\n\nNothing stops you asking for something that will not fit, so mind the token budget:\n`(w/32) x (h/32) x latentT`, ceiling around 43-55k on 8 GB.\n\nReferences are cheap - I costed the packing in `PackedLayout`\n(`comfy/ldm/minimax/model.py:296`):\n\n| item | rows added |\n|---|---|\n| 15s audio reference | 1,206  (603 latent frames x 2, stereo) |\n| photo at `ref_image_size=match` | ~405 |\n\nAbout **+4%** on a 43.3k budget, so lip-sync barely costs you any duration headroom.\n\n**Keep `ref_image_size` on `match`.** `max` uses a 2048px short edge, and the node's\ntooltip warns that reference tokens ride through *every* sampling step, so `max` can\nbe several times slower for identity fidelity you probably do not need at 480p."
      ],
      "color": "#323",
      "bgcolor": "#535"
    },
